# =============================================================================
#  bypass-ports.list - the ports that must not touch the core
# =============================================================================
#  One port per line. Lines starting with "#" and empty lines are ignored.
#
#  Why: some traffic must not go through the core at all. A Rust server that
#  sends a lot of UDP is the example: the UDP pipeline of the core is the
#  bottleneck, and the packets of the game server get lost on the way. The
#  traffic of these ports leaves the router straight to the provider.
#
#  The file belongs to the user: the installer never overwrites it.
#
#  Example:
#
#      # the Rust servers
#      25565
#      28015
# =============================================================================

# port one per line, for example:
# 25565
